 "corrected_patch": {
  "name": "0766-perf-dsv41-pipeline-the-sliced-SP-Engram-row-exchang.patch",
  "sha256": "bc4c5e7a196eb6312e07044d80648575f3f8ea80d077030ebea99892b45152f0",
  "author": "Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com> (original author and date kept)",
  "sp_prefill_py_sha256": "cd10236f284af1ed43e1d7a00c74971935cc82864a4729a2925ac811de573f1a",
  "applies": "on 0762..0765 in series order; 0767 applies cleanly after it; 0762..0765 + this + 0767 reproduces the measured overlay byte for byte (15 files)",
  "git_diff_check": "clean"
 },
 "verdict": "corrected-meets-mark",
 "reason": "The corrected 0766 keeps #979's mark: project_exchange_rows at T>=6144 is faster than the baseline (candidate-49 without #979) beyond the two-boot interval on both served topologies, slowest rank and rank 0: ring4 T=6144 -16.4% (rank0 -17.2%), T=8192 -18.3% (-17.2%); direct T=6144 -18.9% (-18.1%), T=8192 -14.3% (-15.2%); the original #979 measured -17.9/-18.7/-18.8/-15.0% in the same session. Outputs are bit-exact. Everywhere else it runs the baseline's code: gather_mxfp8 is 1107's grouped PyNCCL all-gather at every T on both topologies, and project_exchange_rows below 6,144 tokens is 1107's serial path. So the only cells where its code differs from the baseline are the four T>=6144 project_exchange_rows cells, all gains. The 13 cells where it reads slower than the baseline beyond the two-boot interval all run identical code, and the A/A shows that reading is the interval, not the code: the baseline against itself (boots 3-4 vs 1-2, same session) reads beyond the interval in 8 of 32 cells on the slowest rank and 8 of 32 on rank 0, and identical-code pairs across arms in 45 of 113 (slowest rank). Miss 1 is removed (direct gather_mxfp8 no longer takes the one-shot route; #979 reproduced its loss at T=2048: +46.3% slowest rank, +18.2% rank0) and Miss 2 is removed (no one-slice side-stream path).",
 "gating_rule": {
  "rule": "project_exchange_rows: under the one-shot RoCE policy, one slice (T < ENGRAM_SLICE_TOKENS = 6,144) takes 1107's path (full-row projection, then(), exchange_rows); two or more slices (T >= 6,144) take the PyNCCL copy_self=False side-stream pipeline (#979's gain). gather_many / gather_mxfp8: 1107's grouped PyNCCL all-gather on every topology and T; the one-shot RoCE gather route is not taken anywhere.",
  "code": "sp_prefill.py: `if comm is None or (roce_rows and slices == 1):` -> serial 1107 path, where roce_rows = the TP group's one-shot communicator offers should_all_to_all_rows and comm = _tp_pynccl_comm() (now returned beside the one-shot one); gather_many reverted to 1107 byte for byte.",
  "how_chosen": "Two corrected variants were measured as arms, with the choice pre-registered in raw/plan.txt before the first run: corrA kept #979's one-shot gather on sparknet ring4 only (gate: runtime.topology == 'ring4', T<=1024 at the 2 MB cap), corrB dropped it. corrA was to be chosen only if, on ring4 at the routed T, both corrA and #979 (identical gather code) were faster than the baseline beyond the interval at >=1 T and neither slower at any T. #979 read slower beyond the interval at ring4 T=512 (+17.1% slowest rank) and T=1024 (+59.5%, rank0 +98.6%), while corrA (same gather code) read faster at T=512 (-30.8%): no consistent win, so corrB.",
  "evidence": {
   "one_shot_gather_direct": "never faster than grouped PyNCCL beyond the interval on the slowest rank in either session: own mark +9..+50% (loss at T=160..2048); this session #979 vs baseline T=160 -7.4% within, 256 -8.8% within, 512 -11.0% within, 1024 -6.1% within (rank0 -25.5% 'gain', own mark -0.5% within), 2048 +46.3% loss (rank0 +18.2% loss)",
   "one_shot_gather_ring4": "own mark: -33%/-24% gain at T=160/256, within at 512/1024; this session #979 vs baseline: +6.6% within, +42.6% within, +17.1% loss, +59.5% loss (rank0 +98.6% loss) at T=160/256/512/1024; corrA (same code): +0.5% within, -13.5% within, -30.8% gain, +1.3% within. The own mark's ring4 gains did not repeat.",
   "one_slice_overlap": "#979's side-stream overlap of the one-slice exchange with then(): own mark loss at ring4 T=160/2048/4096 and gains at ring4 256/512, direct 1024/2048; this session #979 vs baseline loss at ring4 T=512/4096, direct 256/512/1024, gain at ring4 2048. No gain held across sessions; it can hide at most then(), one elementwise RankOrderParts sum.",
   "sliced_pipeline": "the T>=6144 code is the same in the corrected arm as in #979 and so is the gain: corrected vs #979 slowest-rank boots ring4 T=6144 [9914, 10061] vs [9762, 9868] us (+1.8%, reads loss), T=8192 [12630, 12753] vs [12608, 12626] (+0.6%, reads loss), direct T=6144 [8983, 8836] vs [9068, 8759] (within), T=8192 [11829, 11948] vs [11679, 11900] (within); the two ring4 readings are identical-code A/A pairs"
  },
  "served_shapes": "every shape in config/cluster.json uses a one-shot transport (oneshot-ring4 = ring4 for tp4-ring; oneshot-direct / oneshot-switched = direct for tp3-triangle and the switched shapes), so the rule covers serving on both topologies the bench measures."
 },
